  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A circle of radius \\(5\\) is inscribed in a rectangle as shown. The ratio of the length of the rectangle to its width is \\(2:1.\\) What is the area of the rectangle?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\( 50 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\( 100 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\( 125 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\( 150 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\( 200 \\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "200"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2012-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The smaller side of the rectangle is equal to the diameter, which is \\(2r=2\\cdot 5=10.\\)\n\nDue to the \\(2:1\\) ratio, the long side is \\(10\\cdot 2=20.\\)\n\nTherefore, the area is \\(20\\cdot 10=200.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E .",
      "hints": [
        "The rectangle width is the circle diameter",
        "Use the \\(2:1\\) length-to-width ratio after finding the width"
      ],
